\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations with the augmented matrix $M$ which we reduce to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there is one pivot column (the $1$st one). Thus, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are free variables. From the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nComparing this with the second column of $P,$ we deduce that ${x}_{3}=0.$ Now, setting ${x}_{2}=5$ and substituting our values for ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ into the general solution, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{2}{5}.$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272054 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271579 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272054 1069 "q-140306" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272054 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272054 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & a \\\\ 1 & 0 & b \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Given that $D={P}^{-1}AP,$ find the value of $\\frac{a}{b}.$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272054 1072 #uuid "18ab2809-44c