a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{121}{4}.\n$$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272304 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271590 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272304 1069 "q-141541" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272304 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272304 1071 "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${x}^{2}+3x.$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272304 1072 #uuid "95bd7791-5792-59a2-8b6d-63a726449fbe" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272304 1074 "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{x}^{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x+{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}}_{⏟}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe first three terms form a perfect square, which we factor as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating the last term, we get\n\n$$\n{(x+\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272305 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271564 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272305 1069 "q-141548" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272305 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272305 1071 "Complete the square on the quadratic expression ${y}^{2}+14y+45.$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272305 1072 #uuid "1238a204-3e93-5785-8e78-51f3b2b7a338" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272305 1074 "First, we rewrite the coefficient of the linear term as a product with $2$ as a factor:\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 7y+45\n$$\n\nNow, here's the trick. We *add* and *then subtract* ${7}^{2},$ writing the constant term $45$ last:\n\n$$\n{{y}^{2}+2\\cdot 7y+{