) \\\\  & =0.1+0.15 \\\\  & =0.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272365 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271674 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272365 1069 "q-142562" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272365 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272365 1071 "Given the joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ below for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ find $P(Y=2).$\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272365 1072 #uuid "24a20428-6f3d-5f93-ade5-d814c51a6012" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272365 1074 "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.3$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.4$ | $0.05$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.55$ | $0.45$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, using the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2) & ={f}_{Y}(2) \\\\  & =f(1,2)+f(2,2)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.25+0.05+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272366 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271625 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272366 1069 "q-142572" 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272366 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533402 17592186045585 true] [17592186272366 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=